{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Converts Stripe errors into the appropriate Apple Pay error, for use in "},{"code":"PKPaymentAuthorizationResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If the error can be fixed by the customer within the Apple Pay sheet, we return an NSError that can be displayed in the Apple Pay sheet."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise, the original error is returned, resulting in the Apple Pay sheet being dismissed. You should display the error message to the customer afterwards."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Currently, we convert billing address related errors into a PKPaymentError that helpfully points to the billing address field in the Apple Pay sheet."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Note that Apple Pay should prevent most card errors (e.g. invalid CVC, expired cards) when you add a card to the wallet."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@objc"},{"kind":"text","text":"(pkPaymentErrorForStripeError:) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pkPaymentError"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"forStripeError"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"stripeError"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An error from the Stripe SDK.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"stripeError"}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"p